3. Drop apps/danielson from a glob, a test list, or a gate.
   - adv 2 (R16, R18): a nested 0.0.55 vinext copy under apps/danielson in a temp
     tree. The disk-read scan (the APP_DIRS rule) reports it; a scan set that drops
     danielson reports nothing, so the case 1 sentinel that pins apps/danielson into
     the disk-read set is load-bearing, and it holds at HEAD. Guard holds.
   - adv 6 (R18): a sweep whose tree drops apps/danielson against a baseline that
     lists it. gates.sh prints NEW FAILURE with the name apps/danielson, NEWFAIL=1.
     Guard holds.
   - adv 7 (R18, A4): apps/danielson stays in the tree but loses its lint script.
     gates.sh prints NEW FAILURE: lint script removed in apps/danielson, NEWFAIL=1.
     Guard holds.

